<h2>Practice notes</h2>
<div class="check">
  <p><strong>Build the delay record.</strong> A long-custody bail application should chart custody duration, witness-examination progress and adjournment history — the constitutional argument is made of arithmetic.</p>
  <p><strong>Anticipate antecedents.</strong> Where the applicant has a record, propose conditions pre-emptively: reporting schedules, passport surrender, local residence. Courts respond to applicants who price in their own risk.</p>
  <p><strong>Use intervening events.</strong> After a rejection, acquittals of co-accused, further custody and stalled proceedings are the change in circumstances that re-opens the door.</p>
</div>
